.TH HOMELAB-DRIVE-WEB-UI 8 "2026-07-31" "homelab-drive-web-ui" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
homelab-drive-web-ui \- Homelab Drive backend-for-frontend web UI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B homelab-drive-web-ui
.br
(started via
.B hypnotoad
under the
.B homelab-drive-web-ui.service
systemd unit; not normally invoked directly)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B homelab-drive-web-ui
is the browser-facing web UI for the Homelab Drive service. It is a
backend-for-frontend (BFF): it renders HTML/htmx pages, proxies uploads
and downloads, and calls
.BR homelab-api (8)
over HTTP for all data access. It has
.B no direct database connectivity
of its own.
.P
It runs as a Mojolicious application under Hypnotoad and is managed via
systemd; it is not intended to be run interactively.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/homelab/drive-web-ui/drive-ui.yml
Main configuration file (YAML). See CONFIGURATION below.
.TP
.I /usr/share/homelab-drive-web-ui/
Installed templates, public static assets, and the example
configuration file.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOMELAB_DRIVE_WEB_UI_CONFIG
Overrides the path to the configuration file (default
.IR /etc/homelab/drive-web-ui/drive-ui.yml ).
Set by the shipped systemd unit.
.TP
.B HOMELAB_DRIVE_WEB_UI_HOME
Overrides the base directory used to locate templates
.RI ( templates/ )
and static assets
.RI ( public/ ).
Default:
.IR /usr/share/homelab-drive-web-ui .
Set by the shipped systemd unit; useful for running from a source
checkout during development.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.SS api
.TP
.B base_url
Base URL of the
.B homelab-api
instance this UI proxies requests to. No default \- required.
.SS asset_version
A cache-busting string appended to static asset URLs
.RI ( app.js ", " style.css ).
Bump it on every deploy so browsers fetch updated assets rather than
serving stale cached copies. No functional default.
.SS secrets
An array of one or more session-signing secrets. Sessions are signed
cookies; if you run more than one instance behind a load balancer, all
instances
.B must
use the identical
.B secrets
value, or sessions created by one instance are rejected by another.
Required \- the service refuses to start without it.
.SS session
.TP
.B secure
Boolean (0/1). Marks the session cookie
.BR Secure ;
set to
.I 0
only for local HTTP development. Default:
.IR 1 .
.TP
.B expiry
Session lifetime, in seconds. Default:
.I 604800
(7 days).
.TP
.B cookie_name
Name of the session cookie. Default:
.IR homelab-drive .
Set this to an old cookie name (e.g.
.IR mailmasker-drive )
during a rename/migration to preserve existing logged-in sessions
across the change, given the same
.B secrets
value; otherwise every existing session is invalidated the moment the
cookie name changes.
.SS upload
.TP
.B tmpdir
Temporary directory used to buffer an incoming upload in full before
streaming it on to the API. Needs at least as much free space as the
largest expected upload (see
.BR max_size ).
Default: the system temp directory (unset).
.TP
.B max_size
Maximum accepted upload size, in bytes. Default:
.I 10737418240
(10GB).
.SS server
Hypnotoad listen/worker configuration.
.TP
.B listen
Full listen URL, e.g.
.IR http://0.0.0.0:2500 .
Default:
.IR http://127.0.0.1:2501 .
.TP
.B workers
Number of Hypnotoad worker processes. Default:
.IR 4 .
.TP
.B pid_file
Path to the Hypnotoad PID file. Default:
.IR /var/lib/homelab/drive-ui-hypnotoad.pid .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR homelab-api (8)
.P
Full example configuration:
.I /usr/share/homelab-drive-web-ui/config/drive-ui.yml.example
